  "proof_route": [
    "exists_cover_cost_lt: Measure.mono_pre makes every scalewise infimum of Measure.hausdorffMeasure_apply at most muH[d] S, so any bound strictly above muH[d] S is attained by some cover at any scale; last round's null extraction is now its corollary",
    "same covering scaffold as the null case, with cover cost < muH[d+1] S + (k+1)^-1 instead of < (k+1)^-1; level slabs, measurable majorant, subtype-indexed Measure.hausdorffMeasure_le_liminf_tsum pointwise bound, lintegral_tsum/lintegral_indicator_const integral bound and Fatou are unchanged",
    "limit: Tendsto (fun k => 2 K (muH[d+1] S + (k+1)^-1)) atTop (nhds (2 K muH[d+1] S)) via ContinuousAdd on ENNReal and ENNReal.Tendsto.const_mul",
    "K = 0: u is constant on S, and exists_measurable_majorant_of_eqOn gives an infinity-valued majorant concentrated on the single attained level, of integral top * 0 = 0, which is exactly what the bound demands; this also settles muH[d+1] S = infinity with K = 0, where no finite-cost cover exists",
    "muH[d+1] S = infinity with K non-zero: the bound is infinity, take F identically infinity",
    "d = 0: the majorant still sums only the pieces whose slab contains t, since an empty piece would contribute 0 ^ (0 : R) = 1",
    "dimension zero (KLS layer): natural subtraction gives surfaceMeasure V = hausdorffNormalized V 0, the space is a subsingleton so u is constant on S, and the same exists_measurable_majorant_of_eqOn closes it with mu = surfaceMeasure V; the zero-dimensional fibre measure is NOT treated as the zero measure",
    "positive dimension (KLS layer): Analysis.hausdorffMeasure_finrank_eq_smul_volume converts muH[n] S into (2^n / omega_n) * volume S, and ((n-1 : N) : R) + 1 = n needs 1 <= n, so the dimension split is necessary; the two normalizing scalars and Mathlib's 2 multiply to 4 omega_(n-1)/omega_n"
  ],
